WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.977
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:06.277 --> 00:00:09.989
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.289 --> 00:00:16.772
Unit eighteen: Natural Disasters. In this unit, you will give advice about preparing for disasters.

4
00:00:17.783 --> 00:00:18.517
Flood.

5
00:00:19.217 --> 00:00:22.761
Flood means a lot of water covering land that is usually dry.

6
00:00:23.061 --> 00:00:24.666
The flood covered the roads.

7
00:00:25.366 --> 00:00:27.949
Your turn. Say: Flood.

8
00:00:30.649 --> 00:00:31.348
Flood.

9
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:33.212
Storm.

10
00:00:33.912 --> 00:00:36.724
Storm means very bad weather with strong wind and rain.

11
00:00:37.024 --> 00:00:38.942
The storm broke many trees.

12
00:00:39.642 --> 00:00:41.958
Your turn. Say: Storm.

13
00:00:44.658 --> 00:00:45.404
Storm.

14
00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:47.313
Earthquake.

15
00:00:48.013 --> 00:00:50.477
Earthquake means when the ground shakes strongly.

16
00:00:50.777 --> 00:00:52.440
Japan has many earthquakes.

17
00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:56.315
Your turn. Say: Earthquake.

18
00:00:59.015 --> 00:00:59.981
Earthquake.

19
00:01:00.983 --> 00:01:01.729
Drought.

20
00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:04.545
Drought means a long time with no rain.

21
00:01:04.845 --> 00:01:06.403
The drought killed the crops.

22
00:01:07.103 --> 00:01:09.709
Your turn. Say: Drought.

23
00:01:12.409 --> 00:01:13.189
Drought.

24
00:01:14.183 --> 00:01:15.266
Emergency.

25
00:01:15.966 --> 00:01:19.393
Emergency means a sudden, dangerous situation.

26
00:01:19.693 --> 00:01:22.262
Call 119 in an emergency.

27
00:01:22.962 --> 00:01:25.695
Your turn. Say: Emergency.

28
00:01:28.395 --> 00:01:29.547
Emergency.

29
00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:31.412
Prepare.

30
00:01:32.112 --> 00:01:34.169
Prepare means to get ready for something.

31
00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:36.295
We prepare for the rainy season.

32
00:01:36.995 --> 00:01:39.241
Your turn. Say: Prepare.

33
00:01:41.941 --> 00:01:42.756
Prepare.

34
00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:44.948
Safe place.

35
00:01:45.648 --> 00:01:48.554
Safe place means a place where you are not in danger.

36
00:01:48.854 --> 00:01:50.911
Go to a safe place on high ground.

37
00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:54.298
Your turn. Say: Safe place.

38
00:01:56.998 --> 00:01:58.185
Safe place.

39
00:01:59.183 --> 00:01:59.871
Help.

40
00:02:00.571 --> 00:02:03.151
Help means to do something useful for someone.

41
00:02:03.451 --> 00:02:05.625
Neighbours help each other after a flood.

42
00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:08.861
Your turn. Say: Help.

43
00:02:11.561 --> 00:02:12.318
Help.

44
00:02:13.317 --> 00:02:15.386
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:15.686 --> 00:02:18.870
Sreypich, how can families prepare for a flood?

46
00:02:20.183 --> 00:02:22.485
We should prepare a bag with water and food.

47
00:02:23.783 --> 00:02:24.993
What else should you do?

48
00:02:26.283 --> 00:02:28.434
We should know a safe place on high ground.

49
00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.157
And after the flood?

50
00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:34.008
We should help our neighbours.

51
00:02:35.317 --> 00:02:37.920
Grammar focus: Should plus verb.

52
00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:41.406
We should prepare a bag. We should go to a safe place.

53
00:02:41.706 --> 00:02:44.461
Use 'should' to give advice for emergencies.

54
00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:48.207
Now read and listen. Ready for Anything.

55
00:02:48.507 --> 00:02:52.271
Natural disasters include floods, storms, earthquakes and droughts.

56
00:02:53.583 --> 00:02:57.034
In Cambodia, floods often happen in the rainy season.

57
00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:02.590
Families should prepare an emergency bag with water, food and a torch.

58
00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:06.521
Everyone should know a safe place to go.

59
00:03:07.817 --> 00:03:10.803
After a disaster, communities help each other.

60
00:03:12.117 --> 00:03:14.676
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:14.976 --> 00:03:17.069
We blank prepare an emergency bag.

62
00:03:17.369 --> 00:03:20.511
A, should. B, shoulds. C, should to.

63
00:03:24.517 --> 00:03:26.377
The answer is A: should.

64
00:03:27.883 --> 00:03:30.591
When the ground shakes strongly, it's an blank.

65
00:03:30.891 --> 00:03:35.230
A, earthquake. B, flood. C, drought.

66
00:03:39.217 --> 00:03:41.030
The answer is A: earthquake.

67
00:03:42.517 --> 00:03:45.654
A sudden, dangerous situation is an blank.

68
00:03:45.954 --> 00:03:49.724
A, emergency. B, safe place. C, storm.

69
00:03:53.717 --> 00:03:56.018
The answer is A: emergency.

70
00:03:57.517 --> 00:04:01.156
Now it's your turn to speak. How can families prepare for a flood?

71
00:04:06.456 --> 00:04:12.359
Families should prepare a bag with food, water and medicine. They should also know where the nearest safe place is.

72
00:04:12.659 --> 00:04:14.345
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:19.210
Great work today! You learned eight new words and should plus verb.

74
00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:23.764
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

75
00:04:24.064 --> 00:04:26.705
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:27.005 --> 00:04:29.750
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

